  "lookup_note": "Entries marked lookup_only are modern materials (plastic, aluminum, nylon, vinyl, fiberglass, chromium) that none of the five historical styles uses. They resolve to their AAT concept, so these values in the data are linked and searchable, but they are never offered to the model or accepted from it.",
  "semantic_rule": "Assign a material only to manufactured objects. A living being, a real animal, a growing plant or food has no material: return an empty list rather than forcing a biological substance such as fur, flesh or hide. Judge what the artwork depicts, not what the object name usually means - a toy cow, a marble statue of a cupid and a stuffed bird are all made objects.",
  "composite_rule": "An object made of several materials lists each one separately - [\"wood\", \"canvas\"], never \"wood and canvas\".",
  "empty_note": "An empty material list is a valid answer and never an error. With is_made_object false it means the object has no material; with is_made_object true it means nothing the model named could be resolved here.",
